i've been a hardcore windows pc fan my  entire life  and only just started to use and learn  about max a couple years ago  when i started working here at max tech  and six months ago i got my first  ever mac the m1 macbook air and ever  since then i've been completely turned  into an apple fangirl  and i can't blame myself one bit so in  this video i want to talk about my  personal experience with the m1 air  how apple stole the show and if you  should buy one  or wait for the upcoming m2 macbook air  instead which  by the way vadim made a great video on  so go ahead and check that out if you're  interested  and while you're at it click the  subscribe button below to support the  channel and help us reach our goal of 1  million subs by the end of the year  at this point nobody can deny that apple  silicon is on a whole nother level  and setting a standard that is nearly  impossible to reach right now  we've even noticed a huge change of  heart in our comment section about apple  it went from a lot of hate towards apple  calling them overpriced garbage  to now praise and excitement over  apple's new max because of their  game-changing architecture  and low pricing for the performance and  even die-hard windows fans can't help  but admit it these m1 max are so  overpowered that intel stole the macguy  and made ads trying to bash on apple and  it completely backfired  only showing people how desperate and  scared they really are now and if that's  not telling on how good apple silicon is  i don't know what is i have the thousand  dollar base model with eight gigs of ram  which by the way you can get on amazon  right now for only 8.99  which we have linked for you in the  description now nobody can deny that  this price point is  insane for what you get the previous  base macbook air also came in at 9.99  however it was almost unusable due to  its thermal issues  i remember editing a video that max made  testing the overheating issues on the  air  and the mac literally reached 100  degrees celsius  just playing back 4k video in chrome and  when updating fortnight the fans ran out  over 6000 rpm  and the system slowed way down and it  stayed at that 100 degrees celsius for  the entire time and  even when max manually maxed out the  fans it still wasn't able to cool itself  down  all of that was because the fan was not  connected to the heatsink  and it was that way on all of the models  you could spend 1250 on the quad core i7  model  and still not have the fan connected to  the heatsink fast forward a year  and apple's own m1 air doesn't even have  a fan  and completely smokes all of those intel  models getting over twice the multi-core  score  as the i7 this was important to me  because i need this laptop to do  occasional video editing and  productivity tasks  so not only did i need a thin and  reliable laptop but something with great  performance too  not only that but the m1 actually  outperforms every single mainstream cpu  on the market and single core  performance  which leads to basically the fastest web  browsing performance that we've ever  seen  so browsing the web is super quick and  snappy there was never a time where i  had to wait for my macbook  it always kept up with me which a  computer should while i use desktop pcs  my parents always used windows laptops  and those were okay for a while but then  they would start to slow down and have a  lot of issues  the battery health would completely  drain and they would have to have it  plugged in like 24 7  just to stay on i remember my parents  constantly having to buy new laptops all  the time because theirs would become  completely unusable and all they used  them for was web browsing and watching  videos  but after max gifted her a macbook pro i  never heard  a single complaint from her again the  battery life is incredible  the web browsing is super fast and that  laptop is gonna last her a long  long time and not only that but she  won't have to deal with any more  annoying windows bugs  so in the past six months it's now clear  to me that mac os  is so much more reliable than windows  since i haven't experienced  any crashes or weird bugs at all with  the m1 air and speaking of software when  this m1 air was announced back in  november  basically everyone believed that there  would be tons of bugs and issues with  x86 apps  but in reality rosetta 2 took care of  basically  everything and now six months later it's  shocking to see just how many popular  apps have already been updated for apple  silicon  and in my experience every single app  that i've used works perfectly with no  software issues  so i've been really impressed now  getting into some of the hardware of the  m1 air  the speakers are amazing they're very  crisp and clean and they're so loud  they rarely have to turn them all the  way up this used to be a massive issue  with my parents windows laptops  where you would turn them all the way up  and you would still barely be able to  hear them  especially over the fan noise and it's  crazy because we've recently got some  brand new windows laptops in the office  and even those have quiet speakers so  apple knocked it out of the park but the  even more  curious thing is that the speakers on  this air actually sound  louder than the ones on the more  expensive pro go ahead and take a listen  for yourself  and let me know what you think  now i don't use my webcam but i've been  editing videos here  for a long time and i've never seen any  webcam that comes even close to the  quality of the m1s  even though it's still 720p so all of  this comes down to the software  and apple software is unmatched because  the m1 chip comes with a dedicated  isp that fine tunes everything to make  it look great now as far as the battery  life  apple rates it at 18 hours of video  playback and 15 hours of web browsing  so you're getting more battery than you  could realistically use in a day and in  many use cases like mine it'll last you  multiple days before you have to charge  up another couple of additions with this  air  is that it now for the first time has p3  colors like the pro  so it's great for photo editing and  stuff like that and the new instant  awake feature is honestly a bigger deal  than it sounds when you use a laptop  every day  and if you're trying to decide between  the air and the pro here's why i went  with the air and why i honestly think  you should too first off it has so much  more bang for the buck  coming in at 300 cheaper while having  the same configuration  and at first we thought that the pro  would have much better performance  because of its fan  but the difference is so small that it's  not really worth the extra cash at all  since the air is still so powerful more  than most people will ever need  now there are a couple of downsides on  this macbook air for one  it only officially supports one external  display but for me  this isn't an issue because i bought  this laptop to use as  a laptop but if you really care about it  there are ways you can work around this  by using special software and adapters  now the other downside is that both of  the ports are on the same side  which isn't a big deal but it makes it  less convenient for me because my power  outlet is on the right side of my desk  so i have to reach the cable around to  the other side to plug it in  which can be pretty annoying but with  all that said i've been extremely happy  with the new m1 macbook air and i'd  honestly recommend it to anyone  even those who have never used a mac  before however the only thing that you  need to consider is that the macbook air  is getting a redesign  pretty soon and based on renders made by  john prosser and ian zelbo  the people have seen a real image of the  redesigned macbook air this one is going  to be really great we're going to be  getting new colors  likely the same ones that we have on the  24 inch imacs  and this new m1 macbook air is going to  be super thin  with a flat top and bottom instead of a  tapered design like the one we currently  have  and the craziest part is that we're  expecting a white keyboard in white  bezels  but i actually kind of like it since  this image with the black bezels  just looks a little strange and doesn't  fit the only downside is that it'll  likely be priced at 1200 and  up so if you don't have that kind of  money to spend i would honestly not wait  for it and just go for the m1 which is  on sale right now for 8.99 on amazon  the m1 is extremely thin and light  already and the battery life is amazing  more than you can use in a day the  performance is insane being more than  people will ever realistically need  and being almost just as good as the pro  and for that reason being a way  better deal and it's going to hold its  value extremely well for many years  there is no reason not to get this air  and i would absolutely recommend it if  you're on a budget  or if you're a college student and need  it for just simple productivity but if  you have some money and some time and  you really like the next redesign of the  air  that one is gonna be amazing and pack a  lot of value  simply for the exciting redesign alone  so hopefully you guys enjoyed this video  and if you did  click the like button and subscribe to  see more videos like it this has been  angelica with max tech and we'll see you  in the next video  [Music]
 

